<title>GERMANY: Buba revises German Dec industry output down.</title>
<headline>Buba revises German Dec industry output down.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank revised the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT	 Dec 96	  Nov 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +0.8 (+1.4)   +0.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year			   +2.9 (+3.5)   +0.7</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    99.6 (100.2)  98.8</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +0.3	     +1.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   +2.0	     +0.9</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    96.0 (96.8)    95.7</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +3.6	     unch</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   +10.9	    +0.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		   145.8 (147)    140.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted. The percentage change figures are calculated by Reuters from the indices. Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
